************** G E N E R A L   I N F O R M A T I O N *************9237 1451   21
                                                                  9237 1451   22
This evaluated data file is based on a software system built      9237 1451   23
around the nuclear model code TALYS [kon07], version 1.9. It is   9237 1451   24
part of a large collection of isotopic evaluations, all created by9237 1451   25
running the system with either adjusted or default input          9237 1451   26
parameters. This means that the data in the entire collection have9237 1451   27
been tested in detail for many isotopes against individual        9237 1451   28
experimental data, while for other isotopes it is only as good as 9237 1451   29
the global quality of TALYS at the moment. The mutual quality of  9237 1451   30
all individual data files is however consistent: The same set of  9237 1451   31
nuclear models is used and, equally important, the same ENDF-6    9237 1451   32
formatting procedures for each isotope. The data file has been    9237 1451   33
created automatically using the ENDF-6 format generator TEFAL.    9237 1451   34
                                                                  9237 1451   35
The resulting data file provides a complete representation of     9237 1451   36
nuclear data needed for transport, activation, damage, heating,   9237 1451   37
radioactivity, and shielding applications over the incident       9237 1451   38
proton energy range from 1. to 200. MeV.                          9237 1451   39
                                                                  9237 1451   40
All transport and activation data for neutrons, charged particles,9237 1451   41
photons and residual nuclides are filed. This includes cross      9237 1451   42
sections, angular distributions, double-differential spectra,     9237 1451   43
isomeric production, discrete and continuum photon production     9237 1451   44
cross sections, residual production cross sections and recoils.   9237 1451   45
This general purpose evaluation can thus be used as both          9237 1451   46
transport and activation library.                                 9237 1451   47
                                                                  9237 1451   48
A complete set of covariance data is included, which is stored    9237 1451   49
in MF31-40.                                                       9237 1451   50
                                                                  9237 1451   51
**** N U C L I D E    S P E C I F I C   I N F O R M A T I O N ****9237 1451   52
                                                                  9237 1451   53
None                                                              9237 1451   54
                                                                  9237 1451   55
***************************** T A L Y S **************************9237 1451   56
                                                                  9237 1451   57
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   9237 1451   58
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      9237 1451   59
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    9237 1451   60
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     9237 1451   61
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  9237 1451   62
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        9237 1451   63
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    9237 1451   64
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         9237 1451   65
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      9237 1451   66
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    9237 1451   67
stored in this data file:                                         9237 1451   68
                                                                  9237 1451   69
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   9237 1451   70
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     9237 1451   71
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 9237 1451   72
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   9237 1451   73
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                9237 1451   74
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   9237 1451   75
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    9237 1451   76
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        9237 1451   77
- Recoil data                                                     9237 1451   78
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (p,xn), (p,xp),..           9237 1451   79
- Total particle energy spectra                                   9237 1451   80
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      9237 1451   81
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        9237 1451   82
- Residual production cross sections                              9237 1451   83
                                                                  9237 1451   84
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            9237 1451   85
parameterization we refer to [kon12]. If for this specific        9237 1451   86
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   9237 1451   87
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                9237 1451   88
                                                                  9237 1451   89
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************9237 1451   90
                                                                  9237 1451   91
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    9237 1451   92
                                                                  9237 1451   93
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       9237 1451   94
                                                                  9237 1451   95
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          9237 1451   96
                                                                  9237 1451   97
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                9237 1451   98
                                                                  9237 1451   99
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       9237 1451  100
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  9237 1451  101
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   9237 1451  102
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  9237 1451  103
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  9237 1451  104
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 9237 1451  105
to the highest incident energy.                                   9237 1451  106
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:9237 1451  107
                                                                  9237 1451  108
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section: nuclear +          9237 1451  109
             interference terms                                   9237 1451  110
                                                                  9237 1451  111
Obtained by integrating the "nuclear-plus-interference" angular   9237 1451  112
distributions of MF=6.  Note that because of the interference     9237 1451  113
effect, the tabulations in both MF=6 and MF=3 can be negative at  9237 1451  114
some energies and angles.                                         9237 1451  115
                                                                  9237 1451  116
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            9237 1451  117
                                                                  9237 1451  118
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    9237 1451  119
                                                                  9237 1451  120
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        9237 1451  121
                                                                  9237 1451  122
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  9237 1451  123
                                                                  9237 1451  124
- MT5      : (p,anything) cross section                           9237 1451  125
                                                                  9237 1451  126
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   9237 1451  127
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        9237 1451  128
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     9237 1451  129
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         9237 1451  130
sections.                                                         9237 1451  131
                                                                  9237 1451  132
- MT16     : (p,2n) cross section                                 9237 1451  133
- MT17     : (p,3n) cross section                                 9237 1451  134
- MT22     : (p,na) cross section                                 9237 1451  135
- MT28     : (p,np) cross section                                 9237 1451  136
- MT51-90  : (p,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      9237 1451  137
- MT91     : (p,n') continuum cross section                       9237 1451  138
- MT102    : (p,gamma) cross section                              9237 1451  139
- MT103    : (p,p) cross section                                  9237 1451  140
- MT104    : (p,d) cross section                                  9237 1451  141
- MT105    : (p,t) cross section                                  9237 1451  142
- MT106    : (p,h) cross section                                  9237 1451  143
- MT107    : (p,a) cross section                                  9237 1451  144
- MT600-610: (p,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       9237 1451  145
- MT649    : (p,p) continuum cross section                        9237 1451  146
- MT650-655: (p,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        9237 1451  147
- MT699    : (p,d) continuum cross section                        9237 1451  148
- MT700-705: (p,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        9237 1451  149
- MT749    : (p,t) continuum cross section                        9237 1451  150
- MT750-755: (p,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        9237 1451  151
- MT799    : (p,h) continuum cross section                        9237 1451  152
- MT800-810: (p,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       9237 1451  153
- MT849    : (p,a) continuum cross section                        9237 1451  154
                                                                  9237 1451  155
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     9237 1451  156
                                                                  9237 1451  157
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     9237 1451  158
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   9237 1451  159
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  9237 1451  160
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             9237 1451  161
All data are generated with TALYS.                                9237 1451  162
                                                                  9237 1451  163
- MT5      : (p,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   9237 1451  164
                                                                  9237 1451  165
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      9237 1451  166
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   9237 1451  167
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   9237 1451  168
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are9237 1451  169
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   9237 1451  170
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  9237 1451  171
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              9237 1451  172
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 9237 1451  173
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  9237 1451  174
For each residual product:                                        9237 1451  175
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               9237 1451  176
- the recoil                                                      9237 1451  177
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         9237 1451  178
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     9237 1451  179
sections.                                                         9237 1451  180
                                                                  9237 1451  181
- MT16     : (p,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     9237 1451  182
                                                                  9237 1451  183
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  9237 1451  184
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 9237 1451  185
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          9237 1451  186
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       9237 1451  187
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 9237 1451  188
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     9237 1451  189
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  9237 1451  190
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      9237 1451  191
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         9237 1451  192
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             9237 1451  193
                                                                  9237 1451  194
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   9237 1451  195
followed:                                                         9237 1451  196
                                                                  9237 1451  197
- MT17 : (p,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         9237 1451  198
- MT22 : (p,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         9237 1451  199
- MT28 : (p,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         9237 1451  200
- MT91 : (p,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     9237 1451  201
- MT649: (p,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9237 1451  202
- MT699: (p,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9237 1451  203
- MT749: (p,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9237 1451  204
- MT809: (p,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9237 1451  205
- MT849: (p,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9237 1451  206
                                                                  9237 1451  207
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 9237 1451  208
                                                                  9237 1451  209
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    9237 1451  210
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          9237 1451  211
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     9237 1451  212
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          9237 1451  213
                                                                  9237 1451  214
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  9237 1451  215
                                                                  9237 1451  216
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     9237 1451  217
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    9237 1451  218
as isomer.                                                        9237 1451  219
                                                                  9237 1451  220
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 9237 1451  221
                                                                  9237 1451  222
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        9237 1451  223
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    9237 1451  224
as isomer.                                                        9237 1451  225
                                                                  9237 1451  226
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 9237 1451  227
                                                                  9237 1451  228
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  9237 1451  229
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     9237 1451  230
with the TASMAN code [kon12], which generates TALYS runs using    9237 1451  231
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   9237 1451  232
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  9237 1451  233
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                9237 1451  234
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      9237 1451  235
   same reaction channel between different energies)              9237 1451  236
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      9237 1451  237
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               9237 1451  238
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      9237 1451  239
   different reaction channels for different energies)            9237 1451  240
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        9237 1451  241
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              9237 1451  242
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  9237 1451  243
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       9237 1451  244
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     9237 1451  245
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  9237 1451  246
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     9237 1451  247
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     9237 1451  248
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     9237 1451  249
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   9237 1451  250
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   9237 1451  251
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  9237 1451  252
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   9237 1451  253
                                                                  9237 1451  254
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      9237 1451  255
                                                                  9237 1451  256
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  9237 1451  257
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             9237 1451  258
                                                                  9237 1451  259
